menu "DRV8833 basic example"
    config EXAMPLE_DRV8833_IN1
        int "IN1 GPIO"
        default 0
        help
            Exclusive output GPIO wired to physical IN1 of bridge A (Motor 1).
            Logical wheel identity and inversion are configured in main.c.

    config EXAMPLE_DRV8833_IN2
        int "IN2 GPIO"
        default 1
        help
            Exclusive output GPIO wired to physical IN2 of bridge A (Motor 1).
            Must differ from every other configured motor/control GPIO.

    config EXAMPLE_DRV8833_IN3
        int "IN3 GPIO"
        default 2
        help
            Exclusive output GPIO wired to physical IN3 of bridge B (Motor 2).
            GPIO2 is a strapping pin on C3; verify the board can boot with the
            attached circuit. A valid GPIO number need not be free on a board.

    config EXAMPLE_DRV8833_IN4
        int "IN4 GPIO"
        default 3
        help
            Exclusive output GPIO wired to physical IN4 of bridge B (Motor 2).
            Board pin labels/locations differ between C3 and S3 modules.

    config EXAMPLE_DRV8833_SLEEP
        int "EEP GPIO (-1 when disconnected)"
        default 10
        help
            Optional nSLEEP output. Set -1 when not connected to the ESP32.
            Both zero commands drive it low; waking adds a 1 ms startup wait.
            Without this GPIO the module must keep nSLEEP enabled in hardware.

    config EXAMPLE_DRV8833_FAULT
        int "ULT GPIO (-1 when disconnected)"
        default 7
        help
            Optional active-low nFAULT input with an internal pull-up.
            Set -1 to omit the input ISR and fault worker. When enabled, one
            worker task and GPIO handler report a latched event plus temporal
            context. The application acknowledges the signal and decides its
            response; ULT never automatically stops motors or inhibits commands.

endmenu
